# Store text with LF in the repository and let checkout decide the working-copy
# line endings. Without one rule for everyone, the same file keeps flipping
# wholesale depending on which contributor's platform touched it last.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These are handed to their consumers verbatim; Git must not touch a byte.
#
# The app icon goes straight to rc.exe at build time. Git's binary heuristic
# happens to guess right on an .ico, but a guess that ever goes the other way
# costs the exe its icon with no error louder than a cargo:warning. The alert
# sound, the poe.ninja NDIC dictionary fixtures and any image are the same
# story: a "corrected" newline in them is simply a broken file.
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.ndic binary
*.png binary
